{
  "description": "Valid Unicode round-trip across UTF-8 byte-width boundaries not covered by the native suite: 1-byte ASCII (single and multi-char), 2-byte Latin/Greek/Cyrillic, 3-byte BMP CJK/symbol, 4-byte supplementary-plane emoji and math characters, and mixed-width strings. The reported utf8_bytes confirms each value crossed the boundary as encoded bytes.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "take_string",
        "value": "A"
      },
      "expected_output": "op=take_string\noutput=A\nutf8_bytes=1\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "take_string",
        "value": "Hello, World!"
      },
      "expected_output": "op=take_string\noutput=Hello, World!\nutf8_bytes=13\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
